# Cursor Rules & Coding Standards

## Developer Context
- The developer is an AI & Computer Science student building strong Python fundamentals.
- Write clean, modular, well-commented Python 3.12+ code using type hints (`typing`, `pydantic`) so the logic is easy to trace and learn from.
- Prefer surgical diffs and small, single-responsibility functions over monolithic files.
- Never regenerate entire files in chat if only one function changes.
- Before a change that touches more than one file, state a brief plan: what will change, which files, and what stays untouched.

## Engine
- The fueling engine is pure Python in `backend/engine/`. Pydantic is its only runtime dependency.
- Do not import FastAPI, gpxpy, sqlite3, or any other third-party library from the engine.
- Parse GPX in `backend/gpx_parser.py` with the standard library (`xml.etree.ElementTree`).
- `backend/fuel_engine.py` only re-exports the engine. `backend/self_check.py` checks plans; it is not part of the engine zip.
- Follow the schemas and formulas in `SPEC.md`.
- Do not change engine math or golden snapshots unless the task says so. Golden tests and invariant tests must pass without silent edits to expected values.
- Mirror only the lightweight GPS snap-to-track and offline fallback in `frontend/offline_engine.js`.

## Frontend
- Vanilla HTML, CSS, and ES modules. No React, Next.js, Vue, or a bundler unless explicitly requested.
- Progressive Web App: `frontend/sw.js` and IndexedDB. Leaflet (OpenTopoMap) and Chart.js are vendored.
- No external CDNs. Ship libraries from `frontend/vendor/`.
- App-shell requests are stale-while-revalidate. Pyodide and `engine.zip` stay cache-first in a separate cache.
- When a file in `SHELL_FILES` changes, bump `SHELL_CACHE` and set `SHELL_FILES_HASH` in `frontend/runtime_manifest.js`. The hash test names the new digest.

## Dependencies
- Pin direct dependencies to an exact version in `requirements.txt`, `requirements-dev.txt`, and `package.json`.

## Tests
- `python -m pytest` covers goldens, invariants, the engine zip, and the shell-cache hash.
- `python -m backend.fuel_engine` runs the self-check and must pass.
- Do not update a golden or weaken an invariant to hide a failure unless that change was requested.
